// Let the visio-recorder service user power the pendant off.
//
// A confirmed low-battery halt ends in `systemctl poweroff` so an idle Pi
// never sits discharging until the rail collapses mid-write. That call goes
// through logind, which asks polkit, and the daemon does not run as root - so
// without this rule the halt is refused with "Interactive authentication
// required", the daemon logs an error, and the device stays powered. Where a
// PiJuice is fitted its own 60-second timer still cuts the rail, but that is
// a cut without a completed halt, which is the brownout this path exists to
// avoid.
//
// Install as /etc/polkit-1/rules.d/10-visio-recorder-poweroff.rules.
//
// Deliberately no subject.local / subject.active check. Those are what a
// desktop rule uses to mean "the person at the keyboard", and a systemd
// system service has neither a seat nor a session, so polkit evaluates both
// as false for this daemon and such a rule would simply never match. The user
// is the whole subject here.
//
// The user below must stay the same as `User=` in visio-recorder.service;
// change the two together or the halt silently loses its power-off.
polkit.addRule(function (action, subject) {
  if (
    action.id == "org.freedesktop.login1.power-off" &&
    subject.user == "pi"
  ) {
    return polkit.Result.YES;
  }
});
